// Water quality through Create Pipes n Physics (pipesnphysics), which replaces Create's pipe and pump
// transport with its own engine. 1.21.1-neoforge only, the one node either mod is built for. Needs
// Create and Pipes n Physics on runClient: uncomment both runClientMod lines in
// build.neoforge.gradle.kts, or drop both jars into run/1.21.1-neoforge/mods by hand. Pipes n Physics
// 3.2.1 crashes the client on the first windowed Fluid Tank without Sable; set
// fluidTiltEnabled = false in run/1.21.1-neoforge/config/pipesnphysics-client.toml. See
// docs/dev/integration/storage/PIPES-N-PHYSICS-INTEGRATION.md.
//
// Six rows, read with client.command; the answers are the "[CHAT]" lines in the client's log:
// - "seaRead"/"seaCheck": a Mechanical Pump drawing a one-block sea-water pool through an open pipe end
//   into a Fluid Tank. The tank should hold water with water_salty true, and "seaPool" should fail
//   (the pool was drunk);
// - "lavaRead": the same with lava, the control. Lava carries no component of ours, so it flows;
// - "tankRead"/"tankCheck": a tank of Murky water (purity 1) pumped into an empty tank keeps purity 1;
// - "gravityRead"/"gravityCheck": with no pump, a tank of Murky water above a Sand Filter, piped down
//   through it into a tank below: the lower tank should hold Clean water (purity 2);
// - "pumpedFilter"/"pumpedRead": the same column with a pump under the filter and 1000 mB of Clean
//   water already in its output: the lower tank should end with 3000 mB of purity 2;
// - "mixRead": Murky water pumped towards a tank holding 500 mB of Pure water (purity 3) must not
//   enter it; "mixCheck" passes while the tank still holds 500 mB of purity 3.
//
//     python tools/agent/new_world.py 1.21.1-neoforge PipesAgent
//     ./gradlew ":1.21.1-neoforge:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/pipesnphysics-water.jsonl -Pquickplay=PipesAgent

